        prompts: {
          human: "Petteia (also known as Poleis or 'Cities') is an ancient Greek board game of pure strategy and military logic. Featured in the writings of Plato and Aristotle, it is one of the world's first 'Pure Reason' games, containing no elements of chance. Players command 'Stones' on a grid, attempting to capture the opponent's forces by surrounding them from two sides (Custodian Capture). It is the direct ancestor of the Roman 'Ludus Latrunculorum' and is celebrated as a training tool for soldiers and philosophers alike.",
